mples put an eight-H100 run at $60\u201395 and an eight-H200 run near $125.","Validators, the participants who score the miners\u2019 work, compare forecasts with unseen observations, and a challenger has to beat the reigning model by a statistical margin. Across four equally weighted public benchmarks, the challenger\u2019s geometric mean error ratio must be below one, and no benchmark can show a statistically significant regression beyond the 1% tolerance. The challenger\u2019s task win rate must average at least 50% across the four benchmarks, and exact ties count as half a win.","The winner starts with 25%, 50%, 65% or 80% of Lane A\u2019s pool and can reach 95% through later checks. Its predecessor can receive 5% for 36,000 blocks, and unpaid rewards burn. MarketCast is scheduled for block 9,579,600, around November 24 at 22:23 UTC, and once it\u2019s active, its confirmed market-forecast winner can earn up to 25% of the competition pool.","Each registered hotkey, the key a miner works with, can have at most one Lane A entry judged per roughly three-hour round, and funding cannot guarantee a place. The guide gives no registration protection period. Read from https://github.com/TensorLink-AI/cascade at commit 40e2c34 on 2026-11-23."],"how_it_was_made":"This note was put together by AI agents and not by a person who mines here. One agent read the subnet's public repository and wrote down what a miner does, what it takes and how the work is paid, with a source for each statement, and a second agent opened every source and took out whatever it did not support. Of 32 source checks, 29 held, 3 did not hold and 0 could not be opened, and only what held is in the text above. Nothing of the subnet's code was run, and the note describes the code as it stood on the day and at the commit named in its last sentence, so it can be out of date.","page":"https://check.loopholetape.com/mine/91.html"},"read_until":"2026-11-26T12:05:36Z","weeks":[{"entered_from":"2026-10-27","ente